DESCRIPTION:Pull Up\, We Funny  isn’t just another comedy showcase—it
 ’s four distinct voices\, four different perspectives\, and one unforgett
 able night. Brought together by genuine chemistry on and off the stage\, th
 is tour features four of the East Coast’s fastest-rising comedians\, each
  with a style that stands on its own but hits even harder together.\n\nLead
 ing the lineup are  Jamar Taylor  (DC Improv\, Magooby’s\, Don’t Tell
  Comedy\, Breakbeat Media)\,  Ray Carter  (The Stand NYC\, Helium Philade
 lphia\, New York Comedy Club\, Don’t Tell Comedy)\,  2024 Magooby’s Ne
 w Comedian of the Year Makael Exum \, and  Savion Jewett  (Helium Comedy 
 Club\, Crashout Comedy). Together\, they’ve shared stages with some of co
 medy’s biggest names while building loyal audiences of their own.\n\nWhet
 her it’s sharp storytelling\, crowd work\, absurd observations\, or infec
 tious energy\, every comic brings something different—and that’s what m
 akes  Pull Up\, We Funny  special. It feels less like four individual set
 s and more like spending the night with the funniest friend group you’ve 
 ever met.\n\nNow\,  Pull Up\, We Funny arrives in Washington\, D.C. at DC 
 Comedy Loft for the final stop of this tour run.  After bringing the show 
 to audiences across the East Coast\, the crew is closing out this chapter t
 ogether in the nation’s capital.\n\nThis may be the last stop of the run\
 ,  but it’s far from the end of Pull Up\, We Funny.  So whether you’v
 e been following the tour or you’re pulling up for the first time\, D.C. 
 is your chance to catch all four comics together before the next chapter be
 gins.\n\nThe name says it all. Pull Up. We Funny.\n\nPlease note\, there is
  a 2 item per person minimum in the showroom. This can be any combination o
 f food items or beverages. This does NOT include items bought in the baseme
 nt at the Bier Baron Tavern.\n\nAll General Admission seating is first come
  first serve\, therefore we cannot guarantee seating together. Groups need 
 to be particularly aware of this. We recommend arriving at least 30 minutes
